# Prose-word budgets (scripts/doc-form.sh): path=N share=S. N is the measured prose words of the page, so growth fails.
# The macOS VM page (19386 words, no budget before) is split into five pages by reader: the entry page, use, base image, host, troubleshooting. 22611 words in all against 22738 before, with the Linux page.
# docs/operations/macos-vms.md 2133 measured: the entry page (what a run gets, requirements, switches, settings, qualifying Macs, licence, upgrades, removal) and the map that keeps the old anchors.
docs/operations/macos-vms.md=2231 share=3 # 2231 measured (+68 over 2133: the macOS VM run figure and the helper row, share 2 to 3 because the figure is one paragraph line; +30: an alias per old heading so every old link lands on its page row)
# docs/operations/macos-vm-use.md 6510 measured: quickstart, keeping a machine, windows, watching, recording, limits, folders and drives.
docs/operations/macos-vm-use.md=6510 share=7
# docs/operations/macos-vm-base-image.md 4669 measured: preparing, setup by hand, editing a base, the prep proxy, customising, boot-time hosts.
docs/operations/macos-vm-base-image.md=4669 share=5
# docs/operations/macos-vm-host.md 3755 measured: VM count, disk, logins, the shared ledger, backups, credentials, the Mac's controls, what the host can see, the run record.
docs/operations/macos-vm-host.md=3755 share=1
# docs/operations/macos-vm-troubleshooting.md 2101 measured: where to look, symptoms and fixes, and what has not run on a real Mac.
docs/operations/macos-vm-troubleshooting.md=2101 share=3
# docs/operations/linux-vm-sandboxes.md 3405 measured, 3352 before: adds the recording, output cap, AWS wipe and limit rows a run needs, less the folded pause-fencing repeats and the drive restatement. 3424 measured (+19): a runner that keeps recordings refuses a recorded Linux VM run; the gateway records the desktop only behind a runner with recording off.
docs/operations/linux-vm-sandboxes.md=3424 share=3
